init: export ro.carrier from androidboot.carrier

Project: system/core (TrebleDroid android-16.0 fork of AOSP android-16.0.0_r2)

Motorola's bootloader passes the phone's sales channel as androidboot.carrier (seen in
/proc/bootconfig on the device: androidboot.carrier = "retin"). The stock vendor image carries
ro.carrier=unknown in /vendor/build.prop as a default and, in init.mmi.rc, tries
"setprop ro.carrier ${ro.boot.carrier}". Motorola's own init sets ro.carrier from the boot
parameter before the build.prop defaults are loaded (its binary names both properties). AOSP's
init does not, so under this system the vendor default wins and the vendor's own setprop fails:

    init: Unable to set property 'ro.carrier' ... Read-only property was already set

(second DSU boot, 2026-10-10). The stock RIL, rmt_storage, the modem power-cutback library, the
thermal engine and vendor init scripts read ro.carrier or ro.vendor.carrier.

The change adds one entry to init's existing table of boot parameters that are exported under
a second name. Without androidboot.carrier nothing is set and behaviour is unchanged.

diff --git a/init/property_service.cpp b/init/property_service.cpp
index 6be4643..566f1f3 100644
--- a/init/property_service.cpp
+++ b/init/property_service.cpp
@@ -1363,6 +1363,10 @@ static void ExportKernelBootProps() {
         { "ro.boot.bootloader", "ro.bootloader", "unknown", },
         { "ro.boot.hardware",   "ro.hardware",   "unknown", },
         { "ro.boot.revision",   "ro.revision",   "0", },
+        // Motorola bootloaders pass the sales channel as androidboot.carrier. The vendor image
+        // ships ro.carrier=unknown as a build.prop default and expects init to have set the
+        // real value before that default is loaded, as the OEM init does.
+        { "ro.boot.carrier",    "ro.carrier",    UNSET, },
             // clang-format on
     };
     for (const auto& prop : prop_map) {
